% 04_two_voices.gmn -- audible test: two simultaneous voices, GUIDO's
% own { [...], [...] } parallel-voice form (disambiguated from a chord
% purely by each item being its own [ ]-wrapped sequence -- see
% guido_import.clj's own header comment) -- GUIDO has no equivalent of
% ABC's own multiple-tunes-per-file concept, so this fills that "4th
% example" slot with GUIDO's own idiomatic multi-voice construct
% instead of a literal tunebook mapping.
[ \meter<"4/4">
  { [ g1/4 a1 b1 c2 | d2/2 g1/2 ]
    [ c1/4 d1 e1 f1 | g1/2 c1/2 ] } ]
